# Spelunking's second ruling: "If a land you control is simply put onto the battlefield tapped without a replacement effect
# being applied, it always enters untapped if you control Spelunking." Arboreal Grazer puts a Forest from Bot1's hand onto
# the battlefield tapped; Spelunking's (CR 614.1d) is the one replacement of its entry, so nothing is asked, and the Forest
# enters untapped. Only lands: Wizard's Rockets, an artifact with its own "This artifact enters tapped", enters tapped, and
# Bot1 is asked nothing about it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Spelunking
Wizard's Rockets
Forest
Arboreal Grazer
Forest
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Spelunking.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose()
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Wizard's Rockets.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Wizard's Rockets.Tapped = true
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Arboreal Grazer.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Forest)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#2.Tapped = false
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Emerald; Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Mox Pearl; Spelunking; Wizard's Rockets; Forest; Arboreal Grazer; Forest
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#1.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#2.Tapped = false
